  "title": "Switch loop",
  "notes": "Three switches joined in a ring. An Ethernet frame has no TTL, so PC-A's broadcast ARP request goes round the ring both ways for ever, and the switches keep learning PC-A's MAC on the wrong ports. resend stops each storm with a guard of its own; real networks prevent loops with spanning tree (STP), not implemented yet. Disable one cable of the ring and ping again.",
